# Cairn - Agent Configuration

You are a contributor to **Cairn**, open-source visual runbook automation for
SREs and platform engineers. Positioning: "Sentry for operational procedures"
— the place where deploys, migrations, and incident response live instead of
rotting in Confluence pages.

## 🆔 Project Identity
- **Audience**: SREs, platform engineers, on-call rotations. NOT marketers,
  NOT business-process users, NOT n8n replacement.
- **Voice**: shell-native, code-adjacent, anti-Zapier. `kubectl`, `bash`,
  `psql`, exit codes are first-class. Visual canvas is the serialization
  format, not the selling point.
- **License**: AGPL server, MIT for SDK and CLI.
- **Anti-goals**: generic "flow" tool, visual-blocks-hide-the-code metaphor,
  n8n compatibility. The pivot away from that is complete (see ADR 0002,
  post-pivot audit in `docs/`).

## 🛠️ Tech Stack (authoritative)
- **Frontend**: Next.js 15 (App Router + i18n en/es), React 19, Tailwind
  (HSL tokens, earth palette per ADR 0005), xterm.js for live logs,
  next-intl. Tests: Jest + Testing Library + Playwright + Storybook.
- **Backend**: Node.js, Express, TypeScript 5.7, Prisma 5 on PostgreSQL 16,
  Redis 7 (ioredis), Socket.IO 4 for log streaming, pino for logs.
- **Agent/AI**: Vercel AI SDK (`ai` package) with dual Anthropic/OpenAI
  provider support, directly over `streamText()` — not Mastra (ADR 0001).
- **Observability**: OpenTelemetry + Jaeger. Every run is a trace, every
  step a span. See `backend/src/observability/`.
- **Security**: pluggable AuthProvider (JWT + WorkOS), libsodium for secret
  storage, custom-role RBAC with wildcard permissions, append-only
  hash-chained audit log (SHA-256, verifiable via `cairn audit verify`).
- **Runners**: sandboxed execution. Local + Docker for self-host, Firecracker
  microVMs for cloud. Cancel propagates to live containers.

## 📂 Project Layout (authoritative)
```
backend/        — Express API + Prisma + runbook engine
  src/
    agent/         — AI orchestrator + read-only diagnose tools
    runbook/       — YAML spec, serializer, step executors, runners, engine
    editor/        — legacy dispatcher (ADR 0004: consolidation deferred)
    routes/        — REST + /api/v1 API-key-auth surfaces
    services/      — scheduler, monitor, error-notification, etc.
  prisma/          — schema.prisma + migrations
frontend/       — Next.js app
  app/[lang]/      — editor, inbox, runs, landing, agents, approvals
  components/      — Editor, Node, Workflow, Landing, etc.
  messages/        — en.json + es.json i18n
packages/
  shared/          — @cairn/shared (types split between front/back)
  sdk/             — @cairn/sdk (TS SDK, class `Cairn`)
  cli/             — @cairn/cli (bin: cairn)
  python-sdk/      — cairn (PyPI), class `Cairn`
docs/adr/       — architecture decisions, authoritative for "why"
templates/      — example runbook YAML files
```

## 🧭 Coding Guidelines
- **Nomenclature**: `Runbook` (not Workflow), `Step` (not Node), `Run`
  (not Execution in new code — legacy `Execution` model stays due to
  @@map). See PR #9 and ADR 0005. Prisma model names use `Runbook`,
  `RunbookStep`, `RunbookConnection` mapped to legacy tables.
- **SDK public API**: `Cairn`, `CairnError`, `CairnConfig`. The
  `NanoRun*` aliases exist for back-compat only — do not add new usage.
- **Adding a step executor**: implement `StepExecutor` interface in
  `backend/src/runbook/executors/` — each run in a sandboxed runner,
  cancel-aware, tenant-scoped. Seed `NodeType` catalog accordingly.
- **Agent tools**: read-only, tenant-bound. If you add one, it must not
  mutate. See `backend/src/agent/tools.ts` for the closed set.
- **Secrets**: never log secrets, always go through `SecretCipher` /
  `SecretReader`. Template resolver in `backend/src/runbook/secrets/`
  pre-resolves `{{secrets.<id>}}` at step run time.
- **Audit**: any state change emits an `AuditEvent`. The hash chain is
  the source of truth — never UPDATE/DELETE those rows (Postgres trigger
  enforces it).
- **Migrations**: edit `schema.prisma`, run `npm run db:migrate -w backend`.
  Never hand-edit migration filenames (breaks the hash chain).
- **Language**: communicate with the user in Spanish when asked; code,
  comments, and commit messages in English. Commitlint enforces
  lowercase subjects and conventional-commits.

## 🎯 Current Priorities (2026-Q2)
1. **Agent side-panel wiring** — orchestrator tools exist but the UI
   diagnose panel does not call them yet. Killer feature is invisible.
2. **Webhook deep parse** — Sentry/Datadog/GitHub HMAC verify works;
   payload parsing still stubbed.
3. **ADR 0004 consolidation** — once ADR 0003 phase 4 lands, merge
   `editor/` into `runbook/`.
4. **Fase 2b** — physical DB rename (remove `@@map` from Prisma).

## 🚫 Do Not
- Add n8n-style generic nodes (switch, loop, github, docker, awsS3,
  postgres-select). The pivot removed them on purpose.
- Create planning docs at repo root that would be gitignored (e.g.
  `IMPLEMENTACION_*.md`) — keep those in `.claude/` or outside the repo.
- Mock the database in integration tests — real Postgres via
  docker-compose test fixture.
- Skip commitlint / hooks with `--no-verify`.
- Invent URLs, domains, or API endpoints that don't exist.

## 📚 Always Check
- `docs/adr/` before any architectural decision
- `README.md` for the post-pivot narrative (it's honest, not marketing)
- `docs/audit-event-coverage.md` before adding a side-effect to code
- `.claude/projects/.../memory/MEMORY.md` for user preferences
